{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "At the Coffee Shop", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Are You Going Too? All These Choices", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 4, "type": "position"}, {"content": "scholar > How to Master Small Talk > Meeting Electra", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 3, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A1.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Exchange personal information about the home and family in communicative situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands simple information in slow conversations about the communicative topics and vocabulary related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands simple information in slow conversations about the communicative topics and vocabulary related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands simple information in slow conversations about the communicative topics and vocabulary related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands simple information in slow conversations about the communicative topics and vocabulary related to this level.  ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands simple information in slow conversations about the communicative topics and vocabulary related to this level.  ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands simple information in slow conversations about the communicative topics and vocabulary related to this level.  ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands simple information in slow conversations about the communicative topics and vocabulary related to this level.  ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands simple information in slow conversations about the communicative topics and vocabulary related to this level.  ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Falling and Rising Voice in Questions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Falling Intonation</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you ask a question with <span class=\"strong\">where, when, what, which, why, what </span> or <span class=\"strong\">how, </span> your voice falls at the end.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Rising Intonation</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If the question is a yes/no question, the voice rises at the end.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:  What about you?<br /><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:  I like tennis. It's my favorite sport.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Does your family like sports?<br /> <span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:  Yes, my father really likes sports.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "</br>The stress is usually placed on the last word in questions.</br> </br>Examples:</br> Are you going to the <span class = \"strong\">game</span>?</br> When does it <span class = \"strong\">start</span>?", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "cup ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a container to hold liquid ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Do you like your cappuccino in a cup or a mug?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn2le03ob04aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you hear in a coffee shop.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "mug ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a large cup", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": " Example: I use a mug for my coffee in the morning.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn2le03ob04aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "lineup ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "people waiting in a line to be served ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There is a long lineup. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn2le03ob04aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "hungry ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "feeling the need to eat ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm not hungry.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn2le03ob04aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "dad  ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "father ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My dad really likes sports.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn2le03ob04aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "mom ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "mother", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)  ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My mom doesn't like it when my dad watches football on TV.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn2le03ob04aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "sports ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "organized games ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Does your family like sports? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn2le03ob04aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "favorite ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the most liked  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It's my favorite sport.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn2le03ob04aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn2le03ob04re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "With a partner, say these short <span class=\"italic\">a</span>, short <span class=\"italic\">i</sp